BINPACKINGJS · V4.0.1
2D & 3D bin packing, visualised.

A faithful, zero-dependency JavaScript library that packs rectangles into bins and cuboids into containers. Every feature from the README is demoed below with the exact code that produces it.

GitHub
npm
2D algorithm (Jylänki)
3D algorithm (Dube)
2D · QUICK STARTpack2D — rectangles into bins

Pass an array of bins and an array of boxes. pack2D returns the placements and any boxes that didn't fit. Bigger boxes are tried first; smaller bins are tried first.

↻ Reshuffle
import { pack2D } from 'binpackingjs/2d';

const result = pack2D({
  bins: [
    { width: 100, height: 50 },
    { width: 50, height: 50 },
  ],
  boxes: [
    { width: 15, height: 10 },
    { width: 50, height: 45 },
    { width: 40, height: 40 },
    { width: 200, height: 200 } // too large to fit,
  ],
});
